  <block>
    <key>options</key>
    <param>
      <key>id</key>
      <value>rx_bladerf</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>title</key>
      <value>BladeRF RX over ZMQ PDU (H.264 via GNU Radio)</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>author</key>
      <value></value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>description</key>
      <value>Reference RX flowgraph: receives GMSK at 2.45 GHz / 20 Msps with a BladeRF via gr-bladeRF, correlates the access code, decodes the burst header (16-bit length), re-packs the payload bits and forwards the PMT PDU (pmt::serialize_str(cons(dict, u8vector))) over ZMQ PUSH bound to tcp://127.0.0.1:5556.</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>window_size</key>
      <value></value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>generate_options</key>
      <value>no_gui</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>output_language</key>
      <value>python</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>max_nouts</key>
      <value>0</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>realtime</key>
      <value>false</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>run_command</key>
      <value>{python} -u {filename}</value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>hier_block_src_path</key>
      <value></value>
    </param>
    <param>
      <key>comment</key>
      <value>Reference RX for the blade-to-blade link (TRANSPORT="radio"). Must bind 5556 before python radio/reciever_radio.py connects to it. Pair with tx_bladerf.grc on the transmitter. Access code must match the TX (default_access_code).</value>
    </param>
  </block>
